---
import { ButtonLink, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro'
---

<LegalPage
  description="Get help with Lumen packages, Playground apps, documentation, the agent skill, or the MCP server."
  eyebrow="Project"
  title="Support"
  updatedAt="August 24, 2026"
>
  <h2>Public support</h2>
  <p>
    Use GitHub Issues for reproducible bugs, Playground problems, documentation gaps, feature
    requests, and MCP connection problems. Include the affected app or package version, client,
    framework or platform, expected result, and the smallest safe reproduction you can share.
  </p>
  <p>
    <ButtonLink href="https://github.com/santi020k/lumen/issues/new/choose" newTab showArrow>
      Open a support request
    </ButtonLink>
  </p>

  <h2>Security reports</h2>
  <p>
    Do not disclose a suspected vulnerability or sensitive information in a public issue. Use
    <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/lumen/security/advisories/new" newTab>
      GitHub's private vulnerability reporting flow
    </Link>
    so maintainers can investigate before public disclosure.
  </p>

  <h2>Before reporting an MCP problem</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Call <code>lumen_get_meta</code> and record the package and schema versions.</li>
    <li>Call <code>lumen_diagnose</code> and confirm the bundled snapshot is healthy.</li>
    <li>Confirm whether the issue affects stdio, Streamable HTTP, or both.</li>
    <li>Remove tokens, private prompts, repository content, and personal information from logs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Response expectations</h2>
  <p>
    Lumen is maintained as an open-source project. Support is best-effort and no response time is
    guaranteed. Clear reproductions and respectful, focused reports are the fastest path to a useful
    answer.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
